Second follow-up to ADR 0002 (spikes/windows-ip-helper): the interface-row
filtering problem, per docs/agent-state/NEXT_ACTION.md item 5 — the ADR's
other named open question, alongside the double-notification anomaly
resolved in docs/evidence/18-windows-notification-family-split.log.

Added `spikes/windows-ip-helper/filter.go` (two functions:
`isShimInterface` matching a fixed, closed set of 9 NDIS/WFP/Npcap/
VirtualBox/Wi-Fi-filter/Hyper-V-extension shadow-row suffixes; and
`isNeverPresentScaffolding`, a structural MTU==0 && OperStatus==notPresent
rule, not a name match) and `filter_test.go`, which transcribes the REAL,
complete 66-row interface table from
`spikes/windows-ip-helper/run1-observation-25s.txt` (not a sample) as a Go
literal fixture and asserts the filter's classification against a per-row
judgement call made by reading the real data, plus the resulting totals.

Command and result:

    cd spikes/windows-ip-helper && go vet ./... && go test ./... -v

    === RUN   TestFilterAgainstRealCapturedSixtySixRows
    --- PASS: TestFilterAgainstRealCapturedSixtySixRows (0.00s)
    === RUN   TestIsShimInterfaceDoesNotFalsePositiveOnRealAliases
    --- PASS: TestIsShimInterfaceDoesNotFalsePositiveOnRealAliases (0.00s)
    === RUN   TestIsNeverPresentScaffoldingRequiresBothSignals
    --- PASS: TestIsNeverPresentScaffoldingRequiresBothSignals (0.00s)
    PASS

Real, measured result against the real 66-row table: **45 shim rows** (the
LWF/Npcap/QoS/VirtualBox/Wi-Fi-filter/Hyper-V-extension shadow rows) +
**4 never-present-scaffolding rows** (Teredo, 6to4, IP-HTTPS, the disabled
Kernel Debugger NIC — all MTU 0 with OperStatus notPresent, and only these
four among the 21 non-shim rows share that signature) = **49 dropped**,
**17 kept**.

Honest correction to ADR 0002's own earlier prose: the ADR's original
estimate was "~9 real network paths ... three 'Local Area Connection* N'
virtual/tunnel adapters." The real data, once shims are correctly excluded,
shows **six** distinct numbered "Local Area Connection* N" adapters (7
through 12), not three — the ADR's own eyeball estimate under-counted this
family. 17 is the honest, reproducible, tested count this filter produces;
it is not forced to match the earlier "~9" prose, and the discrepancy is
recorded here rather than quietly reconciled by fudging either number.

What this filter does NOT resolve, by design, for lack of positive
evidence: the four "Local Area Connection* N" rows numbered 3-6 (real,
distinct, non-zero MTUs of 4091/1480/1460/1464, currently down,
MediaConnectState "unknown") are kept as candidate-real rather than
filtered out, even though they share interface Type 131 with the excluded
Teredo/6to4/IP-HTTPS tunnel rows. There is no evidence in this data that
they are noise — unlike Teredo/6to4/IP-HTTPS they carry real, differing MTU
values, which is exactly the signal `isNeverPresentScaffolding` is built to
respect (see its doc comment). Whether these four are GNS3/VirtualBox
host-only virtual adapters worth surfacing, or another category of noise,
is not established here and is honestly left as a real open question for
5B, not guessed at.

This closes the "design a filtering heuristic and test it against the real
66-row table" half of NEXT_ACTION.md item 5/ADR 0002's remaining open
question. It does NOT design a full identity/dedup scheme for a real
`WindowsLinkAdapter` (e.g. how `InterfaceLuid` vs `InterfaceIndex` stability
across reboots should map onto `internal/ports.InterfaceObservation`'s
identity) — that remains 5B's job, once an isolated VM is available to test
against real transitions, not this spike's.

Verification:
- cd spikes/windows-ip-helper && go vet ./...: clean.
- go test ./... -v: all 3 tests pass (see above).
- go build -o spike.exe .: still succeeds with the new files added to the
  same package.
- cd "<repo root>" && CGO_ENABLED=0 go vet ./...: still clean — nested
  module isolation confirmed again, unaffected by this addition.
- git status --porcelain: only spikes/ (untracked as a whole, consistent
  with its pre-existing repo state) changed by this work.

Updated docs/product/adr/0002-windows-spike-findings.md's interface-noise
section to record this as a resolved-with-a-tested-filter finding, with the
six-not-three correction and the still-open LAC*3-6 question stated plainly.
